{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "A Comedy of Errors"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Not Again!"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 10}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Understand detailed descriptions of real or imaginary events and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Present Unreal Conditional"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The Present Unreal Conditional is used to talk about what you generally would do in imaginary situations. The result of the condition is unclear and impossible to predict with certainty."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The Present Unreal Conditional is also called the second Conditional.</br> You use the structure: </br><span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">If</span>... Simple Past, .... would</span>+<span class=\"italic\">verb </span></br><span class=\"italic\">or Would+verb ...<span class=\"strong\"> if </span>... Simple Past.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:  <span class=\"italic\">If I won the lottery, I would definitely travel the world.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The outcome is unclear, and it is impossible to know whether you will win the lottery in the future or not."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">If I were you, I would tell her that you are not into online dating.</span></br>You use<span class=\"italic\"> If I were you </span>... to give a strong piece of advice."}, {"type": "example", "content": " If I won the lottery, I would definitely travel the world writing ... and eating and drinking."}, {"type": "example", "content": " I would be in the hospital in a week if I dated someone like her. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I weren't specific, I would have had so many losers contacting me."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I were you, I would tell her that you are just not into those sort of things. "}, {"type": "example", "content": " If I were you, I'd change your pictures."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Expressing Absence of Necessity"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the negative forms of the modals <span class=\"italic\">need to </span>and <span class=\"italic\">have to </span>to express absence of necessity in the past or in the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Absence of necessity is expressed with the<span class=\"strong\"> negative form of have to</span>, not with mustn't.</br> Example: <span class=\"italic\">You don't have to date her if you don't like her.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Absence of necessity can also be expressed by negative form of <span class=\"italic\">need</span>. It is generally used as a main verb in the construction <span class=\"italic\">don't need to</span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You don't need to stay in contact with her."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You don't have to be picky."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You don't have to date her."}, {"type": "example", "content": " I don't need someone like this. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You don't need to date people you don't like."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "psycho"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a crazy or unstable person"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The killer was a psycho."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le10ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear when you meet people online. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "aggressive"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " boldly assertive and forward"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He is a very aggressive soccer player."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le10ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to take a peek"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to look; to glance quickly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I took a peek at the scary movie and then turned away."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le10ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "overboard"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to go to extremes"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Working 60 hours a week is going overboard."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le10ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "wholesome"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "good and moral"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She is a very wholesome person."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le10ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "I'm not that guy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not that type of person"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He wouldn't break your window. He's not that kind of guy."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le10ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le10ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I work with a partner to create two dating profiles."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write in detail a physical description and a personality description of my characters."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write their likes and dislikes and hobbies."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I roleplay my character."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I communicate who is most suited to me after the activity."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Watch a video online about speed dating."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In pairs, create two profiles of imaginary people, one male and one female."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a detailed 